\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Experimental data of single unit limit cycles. } Characteristics of the limit cycles, amplitude and frequency, for separate single units. Top: amplitude of limit cycle. Bottom: natural frequency. The x-axis is the activity parameter of odd elasticity of the unit. \textbf  {\ref {one_node_exp_results}} First unit. The frequency increases linearly with activity. The amplitude of the left actuator (blue) stays constant at first and the increases. The amplitude of the right actuator (orange) has large error bars, demonstrating its variability. \textbf  {\ref {one_node_exp_results_2}} Second unit. The frequency increases linearly with activity. The amplitude is the same for the first two activity values. For higher activity, the amplitude is larger, but it remains constant throughout. }}{25}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
